englishSenses.definition:
v. to cause to separate and go in different directions
v. move away from each other; 
v. separate (light) into spectral rays

n. A gentle slope, or a smooth, gently sloping bank;
   especially (Fort.), that slope of earth which inclines from the covered
   way toward the exterior ground or country (see Illust. of Ravelin).

a. A combining form or prefix from Gr. poly`s, many; as,
   polygon, a figure of many angles; polyatomic, having many atoms;
   polychord, polyconic.

n. The quality or state of being vocal; utterableness;
   resonance; as, the vocality of the letters.
n. The quality of being a vowel; vocalic character.
